This directory contains a modified copy of zju-connect
(https://github.com/mythologyli/zju-connect), which implements the Sangfor
EasyConnect protocol first worked out by EasierConnect
(https://github.com/lyc8503/EasierConnect).

Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3. The full text
is in LICENSE. Termther is released under the same licence because it links
this code.

Modified by the Termther project:

  * The Go module path was changed from github.com/mythologyli/zju-connect to
    termther/easyconnect, and the directory renamed, so the fork does not
    claim to be the upstream module.

  * stack/gvisor/stack.go no longer ends the host process when a tunnel
    breaks. Upstream panics on a read or write failure and calls os.Exit(2) on
    a server-initiated shutdown, which is reasonable for a command-line
    program and fatal inside an application: changing networks was enough to
    make the whole app disappear, silently in the os.Exit case. It reports
    through gvisor.OnFatal instead, and drops packets once teardown has begun.
    Every change is marked TERMTHER PATCH.

  * The command-line entry point, TUN-mode stack, aTrust client, forwarding
    services, container files, CI and documentation were removed. Termther
    uses the EasyConnect client and the gvisor stack, and nothing else.

Nothing else was altered, and every third-party copyright notice inside the
remaining files was carried over untouched.
